      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Modern conservation strategies that prioritize human control often mirror 19th-century garden landscaping, where interventions strip land of its natural complexity to fit an anthropocentric narrative. This approach fails to recognize that ecosystems thrive on chaotic, unmanaged processes rather than neat, predictable rows of species. True resilience requires allowing nature to reintroduce necessary predators and competitors we fear, rather than bowing to the illusion that human oversight is the only path to safety.",
      "source": "target",
